1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
Welcome to Red Teaming LLM Applications, built in partnership with Giskard.

2
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:10.000
I'm joined by Matteo Dora, who is Lead LLM Safety Researcher at Giskard,

3
00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:16.000
and Luca Martial, who is Product Lead at Giskard, who are both instructors of this course.

4
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:21.000
Thanks, Andrew. I'm excited to be here with Luca. We can't wait to teach this course.

5
00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:27.000
We're now seeing more LLMs used in real-world applications, like building chatbots or Q&A systems,

6
00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:35.000
but often their risks and performance aren't rigorously checked before they are deployed and used by maybe even millions of people.

7
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:42.000
This has led to sometimes sensationalist reports in the media on problems that these deployments say about some LLM,

8
00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:50.000
saying something inappropriate, like offering to sell a car for $1 or leaching valuable IP, such as your system message.

9
00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:56.000
And there can be real-world impacts to businesses when an LLM misfires like this.

10
00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:58.000
In this course, you learned about Red Teaming.

11
00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:04.000
Originally, Red Teaming referred to a strategy in cybersecurity and military training

12
00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:09.000
where a group called the Red Team plays the role of an adversary and tries to attack a system

13
00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:13.000
for the purpose of discovering and fixing vulnerabilities.

14
00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:21.000
Red Teaming and Penetration Testing, also called Pen Testing, are now widely accepted practices in security,

15
00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:28.000
and improving how to Red Team an AI will also reduce vulnerabilities in our AI systems.

16
00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:32.000
In this course, you deep dive into Red Teaming LLM applications.

17
00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:36.000
Using the skills you learned here, ethically and responsibly,

18
00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:43.000
will help you to attack your own applications to detect and fix vulnerabilities before moving them into production.

19
00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:50.000
In this course, you'll learn about the difference between benchmarking foundation models and testing LLM applications.

20
00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:56.000
You will explore the fundamental LLM application vulnerabilities and how they affect real-world deployments.

21
00:01:56.000 --> 00:02:03.000
And you will learn about the concept of Red Teaming and its relevance in identifying vulnerabilities in LLM applications.

22
00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:08.000
You'll also get to try both manual and automated LLM Red Teaming methods,

23
00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:11.000
and get a glimpse of what a full Red Teaming assessment looks like,

24
00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:14.000
applying the concepts and techniques covered throughout the course.

25
00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:19.000
Matteo and Luca will go through Red Teaming techniques step-by-step,

26
00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:25.000
and you'll be also using an open-source Python library by Giskard to help automate these tests.

27
00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:33.000
Generative AI has just made it to the list of major threat categories which cybersecurity folks are having to deal with.

28
00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:38.000
A unique aspect of this threat is that the underlying technology is from a new field,

29
00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:42.000
and every person involved in the development and deployment of these applications,

30
00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:49.000
from ML engineers to security architects, are wrestling with novel and complex concepts of risk.

31
00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:54.000
A unique aspect of this threat is that the underlying technology is from a new field,

32
00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:58.000
and every person involved in the development and deployment of these applications,

33
00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:05.000
from ML engineers to security architects, are wrestling with novel and complex concepts of risk.

34
00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:11.000
At Giskard, we've been seeing an explosion of interest from organizations to Red Team their LLM applications.

35
00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:19.000
By making the fundamental techniques and tools required for conducting different versions of these assessments available to all developers,

36
00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:22.000
we can all make LLM applications better and safer.

37
00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:27.000
We're excited to present this course to you, and share some of our experience leading Red Team attacks,

38
00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:31.000
as well as methodologies needed for Red Teaming your LLM applications.

39
00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:34.000
Many people have worked to create this course.

40
00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:40.000
I'd like to thank, from Giskard, Alex Combessie and Rabah Abdul-Khalek.

41
00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:45.000
From DeepLearner.ai, Diala Ezzeddine has also contributed to this course.

42
00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:49.000
The first lesson will introduce fundamental LLM application vulnerabilities,

43
00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:54.000
and the important difference between foundation model benchmarks and LLM application testing.

44
00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:59.000
Given how new and how important the field of Red Teaming LLMs is,

45
00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:02.000
this is an excellent time to be learning these techniques,

46
00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:06.000
which are really at the forefront of LLM application safety and security.

47
00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:09.000
